      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(msteams): cap team-group-id cache with pruneMapToMaxSize",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`teamGroupIdCache` in `resolveTeamGroupId` had TTL-based expiry (10 min) but no size cap. A large Teams workspace with many distinct team IDs could accumulate entries faster than the TTL window.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded a 500-entry cap via `pruneMapToMaxSize` — the shared SDK helper already used by 10 other files across 5 extensions (Discord, Slack, Nextcloud Talk, gateway, webhook guards). One line after each cache write.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMemory bounded at ~500 entries regardless of workspace size. No behavioral change.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Production-path proof — 501 calls through real resolveTeamGroupId\n\nThe test imports and calls the actual `resolveTeamGroupId` production function, mocks only the Graph API, and proves the cache cap works on the real code path:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm test extensions/msteams/src/graph-thread.cache-cap-proof.test.ts -- --run\n\n ✓ caps cache at 500 entries — 501st evicts oldest by insertion order\n ✓ cache hit skips Graph API call\n ✓ negative control: raw Map grows beyond 500 without cap\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  3 passed (3)\n```\n\n### Same pattern, same helper — 10 existing call sites\n\n```\nDiscord:    extensions/discord/src/monitor/message-channel-info.ts:53\nNextcloud:  extensions/nextcloud-talk/src/room-info.ts:35\nSlack:      extensions/slack/src/channel-type.ts:35\nSlack:      extensions/slack/src/monitor/thread-resolution.ts:99\nSlack:      extensions/slack/src/monitor/thread.ts:43\nGateway:    src/infra/dedupe.ts:50\nSDK:        src/plugin-sdk/webhook-memory-guards.ts (3 call sites)\nSDK:        src/plugin-sdk/webhook-request-guards.ts:135\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
